      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yesterday it happened again and I was asking the person it happened to, to stay by my side to stay a moment for a test. Appearently, switching out and switching back into the avatar _does not help_ , the avatar state on remote (two people saw me fine, he saw an all 0 state) for him _did stay at an all 0 state_, with only active via the menu or parameter driver changed values getting synced. We are already trying to make \"loadchecks\", to ensure nothing happens until the avatar is completely loaded locally, but due to their nature of _actively changing the parameter for their check_ they get synced and therefore they are getting completely bypassed. \nSo, as switching out and back into the avatar does not work, i did try to press \"reset avatar\" and beginning from that point, everything got synced properly for that person again as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-11T17:27:46.119Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It does seem, that at some point during the beta the syncing of parameters to remote users became unreliable, meaning the avatar would in some cases either execute parameters from an old avatar for a short while, or all parameters are stuck at 0 and only newly \"changed\" ones would get synchronised on remote.\nExample local:\nfloat = 0.3\nint = 2\nbool = false\non remote:\nfloat = 0\nint = 0\nbool = false\nif I would toggle the bool now, local would have the values corretly, but remote would still have 0 on the float and int, only bool would be set to true.\nI have seen it (well, i was the victim) yesterday, that one of my friends said \"why do you look so weird?\" and everyone else saw me fine, a screenshot did show, that the one friend saw my avatar at an \"all 0 value\" state. Even hiding & unhiding the avatar did not help. (Instance was hosted on europe servers if it is important)",
